IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra-definitions`

-- wra3-pt7-final.l4: the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, Part 7 (Final), sections 147 to 151.
-- Part wra3, layer 1. Written from inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk (version
-- 2026-07-01), not the official text. Only two provisions of Part 7 carry a rule: section 148 (financial provision) and
-- section 150(3) (the day appointed by order for the rest of the Act; seam 10 of PLAN.md: wra1, wra2 and Schedule 10
-- paragraph 1(2) take that day as an input). Sections 147, 149, 150(1)-(2), 150(4) and 151 are machinery (inert, reason 2).

§ `s 148 Financial provision`

-- There shall be paid out of money provided by Parliament (a) sums paid by the Secretary of State by way of universal
-- credit or personal independence payment, (b) any other expenditure incurred in consequence of this Act by a Minister of
-- the Crown or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs, (c) any increase attributable to this Act in the
-- sums payable under any other Act out of money so provided.
-- src:2583 | There shall be paid out of money provided by Parliament—
-- src:2584 | (a) sums paid by the Secretary of State by way of universal credit or personal independence payment;
-- src:2585 | (b) any other expenditure incurred in consequence of this Act by a Minister of the Crown or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs;
-- src:2586 | (c) any increase attributable to this Act in the sums payable under any other Act out of money so provided.
@ref s 148 (src:2583-2586)
DECLARE `s 148 sum` IS ONE OF
    `s 148(a) a sum paid by the Secretary of State by way of universal credit or personal independence payment`
    `s 148(b) other expenditure incurred in consequence of this Act by a Minister of the Crown or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`
    `s 148(c) an increase attributable to this Act in the sums payable under any other Act out of money so provided`
    `s 148 any other sum`

@ref s 148 (src:2583-2586)
GIVEN `the sum` IS A `s 148 sum`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 148 the sum is to be paid out of money provided by Parliament` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the sum`
    WHEN `s 148(a) a sum paid by the Secretary of State by way of universal credit or personal independence payment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 148(b) other expenditure incurred in consequence of this Act by a Minister of the Crown or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 148(c) an increase attributable to this Act in the sums payable under any other Act out of money so provided` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the section says what "shall be paid out of money provided by Parliament"; it does not say that no other sum is
    WHEN `s 148 any other sum` THEN NOTHING

§ `s 150 Commencement`

-- (3) The remaining provisions of this Act come into force on such day as the Secretary of State may by order made by
-- statutory instrument appoint. (4)(b)(iii) allows different days for different areas for any provision of Part 4
-- (personal independence payment): the caller supplies the day appointed for the area the person is in.
-- src:2619 | (3) The remaining provisions of this Act come into force on such day as the Secretary of State may by order made by statutory instrument appoint.
@ref s 150(3) (src:2619)
GIVEN `the day the Secretary of State has appointed by order for the provision, in the area concerned` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 150(3) the day appointed for the coming into force of the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the Secretary of State has appointed by order for the provision, in the area concerned`
    WHEN JUST d  THEN JUST d
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the day is appointed by order, and the orders are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@ref s 150(3) (src:2619)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
      `the day the Secretary of State has appointed by order for the provision, in the area concerned` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 150(3) the provision is in force on the date` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 150(3) the day appointed for the coming into force of the provision` `the day the Secretary of State has appointed by order for the provision, in the area concerned`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the provisions "come into force on such day as the Secretary of State may by order ... appoint"; a date before that day is not a date on which the provision is in force (a lawyer's reading (a): a text that fixes the day says no to an earlier one)
    WHEN JUST d  THEN JUST (`the date` AT LEAST d)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the day is appointed by order, and the orders are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
